      "revId": "54b38560f4627064eaff4280aaf2eb575e28df04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca79bcb7_24ca63b6",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 308,
      "author": {
        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-09T15:55:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why isn\u0027t this EL1\u0027s job?",
      "parentUuid": "5048fbed_d7d84d2e",
      "revId": "54b38560f4627064eaff4280aaf2eb575e28df04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "97d5b489_19c23b06",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 308,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T14:02:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If EL2 returns an error code to EL1 then EL1 will assume that the transaction has failed and there is no state to clean up, and has no reason to try to clean it up. Meanwhile EL3 still thinks that it\u0027s partway through being sent. So EL2 needs to make the call to have it cleaned up before returning the error te EL1.",
      "parentUuid": "ca79bcb7_24ca63b6",
      "revId": "54b38560f4627064eaff4280aaf2eb575e28df04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "34fe5200_795b975f",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 308,
      "author": {
        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T14:54:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Aha, yes I see what you mean now, I\u0027ll add something.",
      "parentUuid": "97d5b489_19c23b06",
      "revId": "54b38560f4627064eaff4280aaf2eb575e28df04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7818b427_0811590f",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 327,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-09T15:28:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That really doesn\u0027t sound like a great state to be in. Why not keep the fragments around so that we can roll back if necessary?",
      "revId": "54b38560f4627064eaff4280aaf2eb575e28df04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6ad0121_c7cbe16f",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 327,
      "author": {
        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-09T15:55:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Mostly because that\u0027s a ton of additional state that would need to be tracked at EL2. We\u0027ll need to get there eventually, but in the very short term this allowed to simplify things quite a bit.",
      "parentUuid": "7818b427_0811590f",
      "revId": "54b38560f4627064eaff4280aaf2eb575e28df04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e22949cf_fe56a58f",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 327,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-17T15:15:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ack",
      "parentUuid": "b6ad0121_c7cbe16f",
      "revId": "54b38560f4627064eaff4280aaf2eb575e28df04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "153fedd1_e257dcaa",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 393,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-09T15:28:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If FFA_MEM_FRAG_RX is returned, you also need to check that the sender, handle and offset being requested is what you expect. If the SPMD returns something unexpected (but not a failure) and you need to abort, you should probably call FFA_MEM_RECLAIM to clear up the state in the SPMD.",
      "revId": "54b38560f4627064eaff4280aaf2eb575e28df04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "974f33db_645d7aba",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 393,
      "author": {
        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-09T15:55:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "EL1 can do that no?",
      "parentUuid": "153fedd1_e257dcaa",
      "revId": "54b38560f4627064eaff4280aaf2eb575e28df04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7e3db02c_fe689a94",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 393,
      "author": {
        "id": 1380243
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T14:02:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "EL3 could request that a fragment be resent for some reason, and EL1 would then resend it, but your code won\u0027t handle that. So you need to either support that case, or check, abort the transaction and return and error to EL1.",
      "parentUuid": "974f33db_645d7aba",
      "revId": "54b38560f4627064eaff4280aaf2eb575e28df04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8f58859f_dfa5c1b8",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 393,
      "author": {
        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T14:54:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, but interestingly the trusty driver doesn\u0027t support re-sending fragments, it ignores the offset that it got back and will just proceed to send the rest. I agree we should get there eventually, but we\u0027ve tried to not add code for anything that is not currently supported/needed by the trusty driver, so this is another instance of that.",
      "parentUuid": "7e3db02c_fe689a94",
      "revId": "54b38560f4627064eaff4280aaf2eb575e28df04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1dbb5e8d_f49d0e8d",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 393,
      "author": {
        "id": 1569742
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-11T15:11:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, looking at this again adding the check looks simple enough, so it\u0027s hard to argue this really saves much. I\u0027ll add it too. Thanks!",
      "parentUuid": "8f58859f_dfa5c1b8",
      "revId": "54b38560f4627064eaff4280aaf2eb575e28df04",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9f42fee5_0fdb892f",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/ffa.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 445,
      "author": {
